From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] SystemUI recents: the window keeps its opaque white background

RecentsActivity replaces its window background with a scrim, the wallpaper's
colours at 45 % (no tasks) to 70 % (three or more), and 0 at first on the way
in from home. The scrim is meant to lie over the wallpaper, which Recents no
longer shows: the device overlay makes RecentsTheme.Wallpaper opaque white
and not show the wallpaper, so that ImageWallpaper keeps no buffer
(frameworks/base 0034). With the scrim over nothing, Recents became a
translucent full-screen layer (isOpaque=0): screenshots of it were grey 178
(Test V45). On the panel it stayed white only because the device composer
puts white paper behind the bottom layer (composer/LumaCompose.cpp); every
frame of Recents was still blended over the whole screen instead of copied.

The window now keeps its theme's background. The scrims and their alpha
animations stay, drawn nowhere. Multi-window, where Recents used a second
scrim, is off on a low-RAM device.

--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/recents/views/RecentsView.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/recents/views/RecentsView.java
@@ -310,13 +310,12 @@
      * Returns the window background scrim.
      */
     public void updateBackgroundScrim(Window window, boolean isInMultiWindow) {
-        if (isInMultiWindow) {
-            mBackgroundScrim.setCallback(null);
-            window.setBackgroundDrawable(mMultiWindowBackgroundScrim);
-        } else {
-            mMultiWindowBackgroundScrim.setCallback(null);
-            window.setBackgroundDrawable(mBackgroundScrim);
-        }
+        // PW3: the window keeps the opaque white background of its theme (device overlay,
